===Governors and Mayor of Buenos Aires===

Provincial officials in all districts except Corrientes Province, were elected, as well as the Chief of Government of the City of Buenos Aires. The Justicialist Party wrested two governorships from the UCR (Chubut and Entre Ríos Provinces), and the UCR recovered Tierra del Fuego from the Justicialists.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://towsa.com/andy/totalpais/2003g.html|title=Gobernador electo (2003)|publisher=Atlas Electoral de Andy Tow|access-date=2012-06-22|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120307202159/http://towsa.com/andy/totalpais/2003g.html|archive-date=2012-03-07|url-status=dead}}</ref>

